silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_concrete_anchor#theoremtikzcdfigure a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.00_whitepaper.sections.04_shared_diagram.concrete_anchor#theoremtikzcdfigure" .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_concrete_anchor#theoremtikzcdfigure silm:hasLongDescription "The TheoremTikzcdFigure is F_formal: the formal view functor that renders the Mittens cocone claim as the tikzcd commutative diagram showing twelve typed legs, theorem statement, and proof in section 02_mittens_anchor. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'F_formal', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_concrete_anchor#sharedmittenspicturefigure a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.00_whitepaper.sections.04_shared_diagram.concrete_anchor#sharedmittenspicturefigure" .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_concrete_anchor#sharedmittenspicturefigure silm:hasLongDescription "The SharedMittensPictureFigure is F_diagram: the diagram view functor that renders the Mittens cocone claim as the shared TikZ picture figure SilMittensColimitCoconeDiagram from src/shared/components/diagrams/grammar.tex. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'F_diagram', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_concrete_anchor#plainenglishparagraph a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.00_whitepaper.sections.04_shared_diagram.concrete_anchor#plainenglishparagraph" .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_concrete_anchor#plainenglishparagraph silm:hasLongDescription "The PlainEnglishParagraph is F_reader: the reader view functor that renders the Mittens cocone claim as the plain-English summary paragraph beginning 'Mittens-the-cat is assembled from twelve distinct typed observations...'. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'F_reader', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_concrete_anchor#witnessescsvtable a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.00_whitepaper.sections.04_shared_diagram.concrete_anchor#witnessescsvtable" .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_concrete_anchor#witnessescsvtable silm:hasLongDescription "The WitnessesCSVTable is F_source: the source view functor that renders the Mittens cocone claim as the witnesses.csv ledger rows listing VetRecord_77, MicrochipID_44, DomesticCat, FelisCatusTSN183798, and the nine remaining typed legs." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_concrete_anchor#comparisonmapkappa a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.00_whitepaper.sections.04_shared_diagram.concrete_anchor#comparisonmapkappa" .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_concrete_anchor#comparisonmapkappa silm:hasLongDescription "The ComparisonMapKappa is kappa: the comparison map from colim(F_v circ D_Mittens) to F_v(MittensColimitApex) for each view v; for the multi-view agreement law, kappa must be an isomorphism for each view. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'kappa', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_concrete_anchor#mittenscolimitapex a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.00_whitepaper.sections.04_shared_diagram.concrete_anchor#mittenscolimitapex" .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_concrete_anchor#mittenscolimitapex silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensColimitApex is MultiViewApex: the Mittens colimit apex colim D_Mittens; the single point at which all four synchronized views must agree via the comparison maps kappa_formal, kappa_diagram, kappa_reader, kappa_source." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_concrete_anchor#twelvelegcoconetheorem a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.00_whitepaper.sections.04_shared_diagram.concrete_anchor#twelvelegcoconetheorem" .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_concrete_anchor#twelvelegcoconetheorem silm:hasLongDescription "The TwelveLegCoconeTheorem is DenseClaimExample: the twelve-leg cocone theorem in 02_mittens_anchor is the canonical dense claim that requires all four synchronized views; the VetRecord_77 table, the tikzcd diagram, the plain-English summary, and the witnesses.csv rows are its four synchronized views." .
